    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could act as adaptable tutors: breaking down proofs into visual metaphors (like cooking analogies), or generating interactive exercises based on a student’s neuroticism score (e.g., shorter questions if anxious). Their openness makes them great for creative applications—like explaining graph theory through board games. Pairing them with part-time teaching could bridge gaps where conscientiousness frustrates linear lectures."
